1
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:07,333
[ALARM
SNOOZE]

2
00:00:14,033 --> 00:00:15,167
Shoot!

3
00:00:17,067 --> 00:00:20,000
My name is Suzuki Hajime,
a high school sophomore.

4
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:21,267
All set!

5
00:00:21,933 --> 00:00:24,700
My hobbies are daydreaming
and writing fiction.

6
00:00:28,867 --> 00:00:30,733
My favorite genre is BL.

7
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:37,167
Not long ago, I thought BL
was just a hobby of mine...

8
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:40,100
There we go!

9
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:41,233
But now...

10
00:00:45,233 --> 00:00:46,267
Morning, everyone!

11
00:00:47,067 --> 00:00:48,800
Morning, Suzuki.

12
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:51,520
- We gotta get our act together today.
- Totally.

13
00:00:54,900 --> 00:00:56,200
Good morning, Suzuki.

14
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:57,733
Whoa, you scared me!

15
00:00:58,233 --> 00:00:59,900
Morning, Serizawa.

16
00:01:03,033 --> 00:01:06,700
Because right now, there's a
guy that I'm in love with, too.

17
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:09,300
How's the novel coming
along? Making progress?

18
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:12,400
Yeah, I'm almost finished.

19
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:15,000
Really? That's awesome!

20
00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:16,600
Serizawa Haruto...

21
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:17,833
Morning, Serizawa.

22
00:01:17,933 --> 00:01:18,933
Morning.

23
00:01:19,033 --> 00:01:22,700
He's bright, warm...

24
00:01:23,833 --> 00:01:25,267
He's everyone's ray of sunshine.

25
00:01:26,700 --> 00:01:31,900
Of course, I know it's a love
that will never go anywhere.

26
00:01:33,967 --> 00:01:35,533
Even so...

27
00:01:37,467 --> 00:01:39,400
[BL NOVEL: THE END]

28
00:01:41,567 --> 00:01:44,867
I... I finished it.

29
00:01:44,967 --> 00:01:46,267
Yes!

30
00:01:47,533 --> 00:01:48,900
Oh, Serizawa...

31
00:01:53,533 --> 00:01:56,833
I should just tell him in person.

32
00:01:58,467 --> 00:02:02,700
Even if I can never tell him how I feel...

33
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:08,533
I want to see him so badly...

34
00:02:12,433 --> 00:02:14,767
Serizawa is still the person I love most.

35
00:02:55,333 --> 00:02:58,200
"Popular Serizawa Acts Weird Around Me"

36
00:02:59,833 --> 00:03:02,733
[Episode 10]

37
00:03:02,833 --> 00:03:04,000
All right!

38
00:03:04,167 --> 00:03:05,733
- Hey!
- Serizawa!

39
00:03:05,933 --> 00:03:07,067
Look out!

40
00:03:07,167 --> 00:03:08,167
Huh...?

41
00:03:08,300 --> 00:03:09,300
Hey!

42
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:10,567
Morning.

43
00:03:12,253 --> 00:03:13,486
Where's Serizawa?

44
00:03:13,700 --> 00:03:14,333
Serizawa?

45
00:03:14,433 --> 00:03:18,033
[Good morning. Are you coming to school today?
There's something I want to tell you...]

46
00:03:20,933 --> 00:03:23,933
Suzuki, you've been
glued to your phone all day.

47
00:03:24,033 --> 00:03:24,733
Huh?

48
00:03:24,833 --> 00:03:26,900
Are you really that lonely
without Serizawa around?

49
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:31,667
Yeah... I really miss him.

50
00:03:33,067 --> 00:03:34,700
Aww, he really does!

51
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:42,000
Actually, I finished my novel last night...

52
00:03:42,100 --> 00:03:45,067
The one you're always working on here?

53
00:03:45,167 --> 00:03:46,067
Yeah.

54
00:03:46,167 --> 00:03:48,700
Really? That's incredible! Good for you!

55
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:50,033
Yeah, thanks.

56
00:03:50,133 --> 00:03:51,633
By the way, I've always wondered...

57
00:03:51,733 --> 00:03:54,000
What's your story about anyway, Suzuki?

58
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:55,833
I want to know, too!

59
00:03:55,933 --> 00:03:57,400
Well...

60
00:04:00,200 --> 00:04:03,667
The protagonist is kind of a loner...

61
00:04:04,367 --> 00:04:06,767
He has zero confidence in himself...

62
00:04:08,233 --> 00:04:12,500
Then he gets close to one
of the popular kids at school...

63
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:15,200
They fall in love...

64
00:04:17,267 --> 00:04:19,233
And they start chasing
their dreams together...

65
00:04:20,667 --> 00:04:22,333
That's pretty much it.

66
00:04:24,300 --> 00:04:25,767
Whoa...

67
00:04:26,433 --> 00:04:28,200
So that's the kind of story it is!

68
00:04:29,033 --> 00:04:31,367
We'd love to read it, too.

69
00:04:31,467 --> 00:04:32,467
Totally.

70
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:33,633
Wait, really?

71
00:04:33,733 --> 00:04:35,400
Yeah, definitely! Right, guys?

72
00:04:35,500 --> 00:04:37,667
- Yeah.
- I want to read it, too!

73
00:04:37,767 --> 00:04:38,767
Sure, of course.

74
00:04:38,833 --> 00:04:39,833
No way, really?!

75
00:04:39,933 --> 00:04:41,533
- Let's see it!
- Show us!

76
00:04:41,633 --> 00:04:44,033
- Sweet!
- I can't wait!

77
00:04:44,900 --> 00:04:46,633
Wait, hold on a second.

78
00:04:47,033 --> 00:04:48,033
Huh?

79
00:04:48,067 --> 00:04:53,233
Um... I want Serizawa to read it first.

80
00:04:54,567 --> 00:04:56,800
Can I show you guys after he finishes?

81
00:05:00,533 --> 00:05:02,733
Why are you all grinning like that?

82
00:05:02,833 --> 00:05:03,833
Oh, nothing...

83
00:05:03,933 --> 00:05:07,067
Just wondering why Serizawa
has to be the very first.

84
00:05:07,167 --> 00:05:13,867
Because... Serizawa is my... first reader.

85
00:05:13,967 --> 00:05:16,767
Oh, your first reader, is he?

86
00:05:18,867 --> 00:05:20,227
Is that really all there is to it?

87
00:05:25,446 --> 00:05:27,446
- Well, can't argue with that.
- Yeah, fair enough.

88
00:05:28,100 --> 00:05:29,176
Then I call being reader number two!

89
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:30,967
Then I'll be reader number three!

90
00:05:38,700 --> 00:05:40,033
Still no reply...

91
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:46,367
Hey, Suzuki, what's up?

92
00:05:46,467 --> 00:05:49,333
Oh, I'm here to turn in
the cultural festival surveys...

93
00:05:49,433 --> 00:05:51,067
Oh, thanks a lot.

94
00:05:52,233 --> 00:05:53,367
By the way...

95
00:05:53,467 --> 00:05:57,267
Could you take those photos over there
and put them up in the classroom for me?

96
00:05:57,367 --> 00:05:59,067
Thanks.

97
00:05:59,667 --> 00:06:01,967
The cultural festival was so much fun.

98
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:06,133
It turned out so lively
thanks to all your hard work.

99
00:06:08,513 --> 00:06:12,033
Still, when I first stepped
up and volunteered...

100
00:06:12,133 --> 00:06:14,367
I must have caused you
a lot of worry, Teacher.

101
00:06:14,467 --> 00:06:15,567
Huh?

102
00:06:15,667 --> 00:06:16,867
Because...

103
00:06:16,967 --> 00:06:19,100
Someone gloomy like me...

104
00:06:19,200 --> 00:06:21,933
taking on the festival
executive committee...

105
00:06:22,033 --> 00:06:26,533
I just wasn't cut out for it. I'm
sure I seemed totally unreliable.

106
00:06:27,467 --> 00:06:30,033
I wish I could be more like Serizawa.

107
00:06:32,300 --> 00:06:33,700
You think so?

108
00:06:34,233 --> 00:06:37,300
I thought it suited you well.
You were very dependable.

109
00:06:39,533 --> 00:06:40,900
You know...

110
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:43,567
Calling people 'gloomy' or 'cheerful'...

111
00:06:44,367 --> 00:06:46,233
or obsessing over MBTI types...

112
00:06:47,267 --> 00:06:51,600
people love boxing
themselves into little categories.

113
00:06:53,167 --> 00:06:57,067
But people aren't nearly that simple.

114
00:07:00,133 --> 00:07:04,700
Everyone carries so many
different sides within them.

115
00:07:05,333 --> 00:07:07,767
There are things you can't
even tell your closest friends.

116
00:07:09,033 --> 00:07:10,200
Don't worry about it.

117
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:12,620
There are sides you only ever
show to the person you love.

118
00:07:13,133 --> 00:07:14,667
It's all good, really.

119
00:07:14,767 --> 00:07:17,667
Look, Teacher Usami's
proposal video went viral!

120
00:07:17,767 --> 00:07:19,067
Wait, are you serious?!

121
00:07:19,167 --> 00:07:20,800
No freaking way!

122
00:07:23,167 --> 00:07:26,567
And there are people agonizing over
things in private, where no one sees.

123
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:31,500
Still on your mind?

124
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:35,700
Stop rubbing salt on the wound.

125
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:44,667
So there's really no need...

126
00:07:45,267 --> 00:07:48,633
to decide who you are before
you even give yourself a chance.

127
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:51,833
Besides...

128
00:07:52,706 --> 00:07:55,006
as far as I can tell, even Serizawa...

129
00:07:55,100 --> 00:07:58,367
clearly acts weird whenever
he's around you, Suzuki.

130
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,900
Around me...?

131
00:08:08,167 --> 00:08:09,867
Oh, excuse me for a moment...

132
00:08:12,100 --> 00:08:13,600
Hello, Serizawa? What's up?

133
00:08:13,700 --> 00:08:15,233
Suzuki, are you okay?

134
00:08:15,333 --> 00:08:16,367
Wait, what?

135
00:08:16,467 --> 00:08:18,133
I just saw your message...

136
00:08:18,233 --> 00:08:19,609
You said you needed to talk to me...

137
00:08:19,633 --> 00:08:21,343
I thought something
terrible happened to you...

138
00:08:21,367 --> 00:08:22,533
So, what did you want to say?

139
00:08:22,633 --> 00:08:24,776
Is it good news? Bad news? Did
something happen, or is it something good?

140
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:27,400
No, nothing like that... Serizawa,
just calm down for a second...

141
00:08:27,800 --> 00:08:29,143
Wait, where are you right now anyway?

142
00:08:29,167 --> 00:08:31,433
Me? I just got to school...

143
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:36,333
Suzuki!

144
00:08:37,300 --> 00:08:39,433
Are you really okay?
Nothing happened, right?

145
00:08:39,533 --> 00:08:40,900
Are you hurt?

146
00:08:41,067 --> 00:08:43,600
Yeah, I'm fine.

147
00:08:45,200 --> 00:08:48,567
Thank goodness... You
scared the life out of me.

148
00:08:49,267 --> 00:08:51,333
Um, Serizawa...

149
00:08:51,633 --> 00:08:57,167
I finished it. My novel, the whole thing.

150
00:08:57,267 --> 00:08:59,467
Whoa, really?!

151
00:08:59,491 --> 00:09:00,924
That's incredible!

152
00:09:00,948 --> 00:09:02,715
You're amazing, Suzuki!

153
00:09:02,967 --> 00:09:06,533
So... I wanted you to read it.

154
00:09:07,300 --> 00:09:09,000
Will you?

155
00:09:09,100 --> 00:09:10,400
Of course I will!

156
00:09:10,500 --> 00:09:11,600
All right, let's go!

157
00:09:11,700 --> 00:09:12,433
Right now?

158
00:09:12,533 --> 00:09:13,167
Right now!

159
00:09:13,267 --> 00:09:14,367
Wait, but we have class...

160
00:09:14,467 --> 00:09:17,200
No! Right now! Immediately!

161
00:09:25,646 --> 00:09:27,507
(He smiled happily as he ate
the tamagoyaki I offered him.)

162
00:09:27,531 --> 00:09:29,766
(This corner became
our very own VIP area.)

163
00:09:32,933 --> 00:09:34,267
I finished reading it.

164
00:09:34,767 --> 00:09:36,800
How... How was it?

165
00:09:37,867 --> 00:09:40,333
Can I tell you the truth?

166
00:09:41,567 --> 00:09:42,967
Yeah.

167
00:09:43,967 --> 00:09:47,100
I honestly feel like crying right now.

168
00:09:47,700 --> 00:09:48,567
Huh?

169
00:09:48,667 --> 00:09:51,700
Because... it was just such a happy ending.

170
00:09:51,800 --> 00:09:54,567
That ending was way too heartwarming.

171
00:09:55,233 --> 00:09:58,700
I can't... I'm so deeply moved.

172
00:10:02,300 --> 00:10:03,167
Really?

173
00:10:03,267 --> 00:10:04,567
Yeah, really.

174
00:10:04,667 --> 00:10:06,367
My heart was pounding the entire time.

175
00:10:06,767 --> 00:10:09,500
And knowing that you wrote this, Suzuki...

176
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:13,067
it just fills my heart
with so much emotion.

177
00:10:22,933 --> 00:10:24,333
What about you, Suzuki?

178
00:10:26,433 --> 00:10:29,433
How are you feeling right now?

179
00:10:32,433 --> 00:10:35,267
Right now... I'm...

180
00:10:37,933 --> 00:10:39,367
just so incredibly happy.

181
00:10:43,433 --> 00:10:45,233
I always hated that part of myself...

182
00:10:46,333 --> 00:10:49,200
the me that could never finish anything.

183
00:10:49,900 --> 00:10:51,833
I couldn't forgive myself for it.

184
00:10:53,233 --> 00:10:56,067
I beat myself up over it
more times than I can count.

185
00:11:01,767 --> 00:11:04,300
So seeing it through to
the end makes me so happy.

186
00:11:06,167 --> 00:11:08,867
And being able to share it
with you makes me even happier.

187
00:11:12,200 --> 00:11:17,267
Even now, it feels almost hard to believe.

188
00:11:22,400 --> 00:11:24,400
Because it's you, Serizawa.

189
00:11:25,300 --> 00:11:27,300
The person I've always admired...

190
00:11:28,667 --> 00:11:33,100
My... everyone's ray of sunshine.

191
00:11:36,033 --> 00:11:39,667
I always thought that someone like me...

192
00:11:39,767 --> 00:11:42,067
could never even touch your world.

193
00:11:43,600 --> 00:11:50,900
Yet you've always
stayed right by my side...

194
00:11:53,367 --> 00:11:55,033
And even for my story...

195
00:11:58,767 --> 00:12:00,500
you're this happy for me.

196
00:12:05,033 --> 00:12:06,233
I can't hold it in.

197
00:12:08,833 --> 00:12:12,700
I'm just...

198
00:12:13,733 --> 00:12:15,467
so happy...

199
00:12:16,400 --> 00:12:18,667
I'm just so, so happy.

200
00:12:20,533 --> 00:12:27,200
Right now, you're right here...

201
00:12:28,533 --> 00:12:31,300
right here by my side.

202
00:12:33,300 --> 00:12:34,900
I'm just so completely happy.

203
00:12:46,333 --> 00:12:52,333
I'm really happy, too, Suzuki.

204
00:13:06,567 --> 00:13:07,767
Huh?

205
00:13:12,267 --> 00:13:13,500
What's wrong?

206
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:17,967
Nothing, it's just...

207
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:23,000
You kind of smell like...

208
00:13:24,233 --> 00:13:26,667
soy sauce, Serizawa.

209
00:13:27,133 --> 00:13:30,267
Ah, you noticed?

210
00:13:30,367 --> 00:13:33,733
Actually, there's something
I wanted to show you, too.

211
00:13:42,767 --> 00:13:44,267
Ta-da!

212
00:13:45,767 --> 00:13:48,567
I just cooked this stew.

213
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:50,200
Huh?

214
00:13:50,233 --> 00:13:53,667
Wait, you don't remember?

215
00:13:53,767 --> 00:13:55,200
Didn't we make a promise?

216
00:13:58,267 --> 00:14:02,200
All right, then I'll do my best
to become the King of Stews!

217
00:14:02,300 --> 00:14:03,300
Ah!

218
00:14:04,267 --> 00:14:07,133
Don't tell me that promise was...

219
00:14:07,233 --> 00:14:11,567
Yeah! When you said your
novel was almost finished...

220
00:14:11,667 --> 00:14:14,000
I figured I had to step up my game, too.

221
00:14:14,100 --> 00:14:18,367
Uh... so you mean...

222
00:14:20,933 --> 00:14:22,667
you're going to...?

223
00:14:22,767 --> 00:14:24,500
Become the King of Stews!

224
00:14:26,167 --> 00:14:28,367
Hey, what are you laughing at, Suzuki?

225
00:14:28,567 --> 00:14:30,433
Because you're...

226
00:14:30,733 --> 00:14:32,167
The King of Stews!

227
00:15:07,033 --> 00:15:08,600
Oh, sorry...

228
00:15:09,967 --> 00:15:11,367
I've gotta run.

229
00:15:11,467 --> 00:15:12,467
Okay.

230
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:27,300
All right, let's call
this meeting to order.

231
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:28,867
Thanks for coming.

232
00:15:28,967 --> 00:15:30,367
Let's do this.

233
00:15:36,733 --> 00:15:38,400
So, what's on the agenda today?

234
00:15:38,500 --> 00:15:41,200
'Regarding the matter of
Serizawa and Suzuki almost kissing.'

235
00:15:41,300 --> 00:15:44,600
Not this again! Besides,
they didn't even kiss!

236
00:15:45,167 --> 00:15:46,733
Meeting adjourned! Adjourned!

237
00:15:46,833 --> 00:15:48,033
Dismissed!

238
00:15:48,133 --> 00:15:50,433
- Let's bail.
- Catch ya later!

239
00:15:53,033 --> 00:15:54,467
Nice try, you two!

240
00:15:56,633 --> 00:15:58,800
Get back here! Both of you!

241
00:15:59,467 --> 00:16:00,867
Something feels different today.

242
00:16:01,300 --> 00:16:02,767
Um... Serizawa.

243
00:16:05,367 --> 00:16:06,667
I'm sorry.

244
00:16:08,433 --> 00:16:12,333
I've been lying to you this whole time.

245
00:16:12,767 --> 00:16:13,767
Huh?

246
00:16:15,667 --> 00:16:19,533
Do you remember back at the beach...

247
00:16:19,633 --> 00:16:22,300
when you asked if I had a crush on someone?

248
00:16:23,167 --> 00:16:26,533
Back then, I said I didn't...

249
00:16:28,633 --> 00:16:30,067
That was a lie.

250
00:16:35,700 --> 00:16:37,800
The truth is...

251
00:16:40,300 --> 00:16:42,500
Ever since that moment...

252
00:16:44,500 --> 00:16:51,800
I've been in love with you, Serizawa.

253
00:16:56,400 --> 00:16:59,800
Of course, I know you
already like someone...

254
00:16:59,900 --> 00:17:01,900
and I know it isn't me.

255
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:02,567
Wait, what?

256
00:17:02,667 --> 00:17:05,233
So please, just reject me flat out.

257
00:17:05,333 --> 00:17:06,633
No, wait a second.

258
00:17:06,733 --> 00:17:08,000
Huh?

259
00:17:09,833 --> 00:17:13,233
No, the person I like...

260
00:17:13,333 --> 00:17:14,800
is you, Suzuki.

261
00:17:17,167 --> 00:17:18,567
What are you talking about...?

262
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:34,867
Um... sorry, I'm completely lost.

263
00:17:34,967 --> 00:17:36,767
What are we even talking about right now?

264
00:17:36,867 --> 00:17:40,833
He's saying the one
Serizawa loves is you, Suzuki!

265
00:17:40,933 --> 00:17:42,100
Yeah.

266
00:17:42,200 --> 00:17:46,367
Seriously, Suzuki, you
had absolutely no idea?

267
00:17:46,467 --> 00:17:47,567
Wait, but...

268
00:17:47,667 --> 00:17:49,267
I heard that back in your first year...

269
00:17:49,367 --> 00:17:52,367
Serizawa got into BL
because of the person he liked.

270
00:17:52,467 --> 00:17:54,467
Yeah, that's right.

271
00:17:55,333 --> 00:17:58,600
He got into it because of his crush.

272
00:17:58,700 --> 00:18:00,700
That makes no sense! Because...

273
00:18:00,800 --> 00:18:03,400
we didn't even meet until sophomore year!

274
00:18:03,500 --> 00:18:07,000
And you were already into BL back then!

275
00:18:08,067 --> 00:18:10,300
Ohhh, so that's what this is about!

276
00:18:12,067 --> 00:18:13,067
What do you mean?

277
00:18:13,100 --> 00:18:15,033
No, see...

278
00:18:15,133 --> 00:18:16,867
Argh, forget it! I'll explain everything.

279
00:18:16,967 --> 00:18:18,267
Come on, Suzuki, let's go.

280
00:18:18,367 --> 00:18:19,700
Where are we going?

281
00:18:20,500 --> 00:18:21,833
Isn't it obvious?

282
00:18:22,667 --> 00:18:24,967
Somewhere we can be alone.

283
00:18:29,600 --> 00:18:31,500
Have fun, you two!

284
00:18:33,467 --> 00:18:34,800
- Thank you.
- Thanks.

285
00:18:36,233 --> 00:18:36,900
First, let's make a toast.

286
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:38,133
Here, cheers.

287
00:18:38,633 --> 00:18:39,833
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

288
00:18:43,400 --> 00:18:46,967
Wait, let me wrap my head around this.

289
00:18:47,067 --> 00:18:48,267
Go ahead.

290
00:18:48,800 --> 00:18:54,367
So you saw me back in our first year...

291
00:18:54,467 --> 00:18:57,000
and that's when you started reading BL?

292
00:18:57,100 --> 00:18:58,100
Yeah.

293
00:18:59,233 --> 00:19:00,433
Wait, but that's bizarre.

294
00:19:00,533 --> 00:19:01,333
Because if that's the case...

295
00:19:01,433 --> 00:19:03,833
doesn't that mean the
person you like is me?

296
00:19:03,933 --> 00:19:05,533
That's literally what I've been saying!

297
00:19:05,733 --> 00:19:07,933
Haven't I been telling
you this the whole time?

298
00:19:08,633 --> 00:19:10,667
The one I love is you, Suzuki.

299
00:19:11,133 --> 00:19:13,867
Only ever you.

300
00:19:14,767 --> 00:19:16,100
Get it now?

301
00:19:18,067 --> 00:19:19,367
I don't get it at all!

302
00:19:19,767 --> 00:19:23,767
Because you're everyone's
ray of sunshine, Serizawa!

303
00:19:23,867 --> 00:19:25,100
I don't want to be.

304
00:19:42,867 --> 00:19:46,200
Then let me just belong to you, Suzuki.

305
00:19:52,300 --> 00:19:59,867
Do you really... like me?

306
00:20:02,667 --> 00:20:05,600
Yeah, I really like you.

307
00:20:08,267 --> 00:20:09,833
What about you, Suzuki?

308
00:20:11,433 --> 00:20:14,700
Do you like me?

309
00:20:17,867 --> 00:20:21,700
Yeah... I do.

310
00:20:24,067 --> 00:20:25,633
I'm so glad.

311
00:20:25,733 --> 00:20:27,733
I'll want to hear you
say it again and again...

312
00:20:29,867 --> 00:20:32,633
I love you too, Suzuki.

313
00:20:34,533 --> 00:20:38,767
Will you accept my feelings?

314
00:20:44,067 --> 00:20:45,433
You're so cute...

315
00:20:45,533 --> 00:20:48,433
Good boy... my sweet Suzuki.

316
00:20:48,967 --> 00:20:50,767
Ah... but wait a second.

317
00:20:50,867 --> 00:20:52,067
I still don't get it.

318
00:20:52,167 --> 00:20:54,333
The fact that you actually like me...

319
00:20:54,433 --> 00:20:56,300
it feels like some kind of glitch...

320
00:20:56,400 --> 00:20:58,167
My brain is about to melt.

321
00:21:06,833 --> 00:21:08,033
All right.

322
00:21:08,500 --> 00:21:11,667
Until you finally understand...

323
00:21:12,267 --> 00:21:13,907
we can do this as many times as you want.

324
00:21:15,333 --> 00:21:16,500
Huh?

325
00:21:16,867 --> 00:21:18,133
That's the whole reason...

326
00:21:18,233 --> 00:21:20,300
we came here to be
alone together, isn't it?

327
00:22:14,400 --> 00:22:17,967
Well? Do you get it now?

328
00:22:24,033 --> 00:22:27,933
I... I still don't.

329
00:22:30,333 --> 00:22:35,367
So tell me a little more...

330
00:22:37,867 --> 00:22:42,267
Suzuki... you're way too adorable.

331
00:22:46,000 --> 00:22:47,267
Okay.

332
00:22:49,033 --> 00:22:51,800
One more time, then.

333
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:00,600
[NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW]

334
00:23:00,700 --> 00:23:01,067
All right!

335
00:23:01,167 --> 00:23:04,500
Today, I'm definitely making
Serizawa's heart skip a beat!

336
00:23:05,200 --> 00:23:07,567
So this is what you're into, Suzuki.

337
00:23:07,667 --> 00:23:09,000
Thanks for the treat.

338
00:23:10,167 --> 00:23:12,467
The one whose heart won't stop racing...

339
00:23:12,567 --> 00:23:13,200
is me.

340
00:23:13,300 --> 00:23:14,980
[THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION]
*Sigh...*
